@page "/playground"
@layout PlaygroundLayout
@using MonorailCss.Docs.Client

<PageTitle>Playground - MonorailCss</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Edit HTML with utility classes and watch the preview and generated CSS update live — compiled in your browser by the real MonorailCss engine." />
    @* This page is a fixed-height shell; suppress the site-wide body scrollbar gutter so the
       playground fills the viewport exactly. *@
    <style>body { overflow: hidden !important; }</style>
    @* Monaco's stylesheet. editor.main.js would inject it itself, but declaring it here starts
       the 309 KB download alongside the document instead of after the editor bundle runs. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/BlazorMonaco/lib/monaco-editor/min/vs/editor/editor.main.css" />
    @* Glue for the WebAssembly playground island (preview postMessage + editor theme sync). *@
    <script src="/js/playground.js" defer></script>
</HeadContent>

@* Monaco (the playground editor): interop shim + AMD loader + editor bundle, served as static
   web assets by the BlazorMonaco package referenced through MonorailCss.Docs.Client. Rendered
   into App's outlet just ahead of blazor.web.js, so the editor JS is present when the WASM
   island boots. Order matters: jsInterop.js sets the AMD require config, then loader.js, then
   editor.main.js. *@
<SectionContent SectionName="@App.BeforeBlazorScriptsSection">
    <script src="_content/BlazorMonaco/jsInterop.js"></script>
    <script src="_content/BlazorMonaco/lib/monaco-editor/min/vs/loader.js"></script>
    <script src="_content/BlazorMonaco/lib/monaco-editor/min/vs/editor/editor.main.js"></script>
</SectionContent>

@* Everything above is page-scoped, so this page must only ever be entered with a full page
   load — a spa-engine region swap would not execute these scripts. That holds by construction:
   PlaygroundLayout declares no data-spa-region, so spa-engine sees a region mismatch on any
   soft navigation into (or out of) this page and falls back to location.href, and it never
   pushes a same-document history entry for /playground, so back/forward into it is a real
   document load (or bfcache restore) too. The header link's data-spa-reload just skips the
   wasted fetch. *@

@* Static-SSR route so Pennington's crawler emits /playground into the static export; the
   interactive UI is a WebAssembly island (MonorailCss.Docs.Client) that compiles utility
   classes to CSS in the browser. Its own @@rendermode drives the interactivity. *@
<PlaygroundIsland />
